.TH CBMAP_CREATE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cbmap_create \- create a BST map with default settings
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

cbmap cbmap_create(ccol_data_type key_type, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a self-balancing binary search tree map (an AVL tree) with the
default memory management and the default comparison for the key type.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
key_type  Type of the keys that the map stores
err       Optional pointer that receives an error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the new BST map on success, NULL on failure.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The default comparison depends on the key type:
  char: the platform's native char comparison, signed or unsigned to
  match how char behaves on this platform.
  The other signed integer types: a signed integer comparison.
  The unsigned integer types: an unsigned integer comparison.
  float, double and long double: a numeric comparison, in which a NaN key
  sorts above every non-NaN key and equal to every other NaN key.
  ccol_string: a lexicographic order equivalent to strcmp.

The map keeps the AVL balance, |height(left) - height(right)| <= 1, so
every operation is O(log n).

The caller must destroy the map with cbmap_destroy() after use.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_create_full (3),
.BR cbmap_create_mp (3),
.BR cbmap_create_ch (3),
.BR cbmap_destroy (3),
.BR ccol_determine_ccol_data_type (3)
